        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Testing backticks in front matter title on two HTML pages]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43486</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/43486"/>
        <updated>2026-03-19T00:03:23.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/23019147?u=4c0de81596ced64dc067dea5686f7ca2912db0cb&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">For standardizing our titles on reference pages, backtick support has been added in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4027145920" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/rari/issues/552" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/rari/pull/552/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/rari/pull/552">mdn/rari#552</a>, which is now available in mdn/content.</p>
<p dir="auto">In this PR, I'm trying out the backticks on two reference pages in HTML.</p>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">rari</code> is correctly outputting <code class="notranslate">titleHTML</code> in the JSON:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><code class="notranslate">"titleHTML"</code>: <code class="notranslate">"&lt;code&gt;is&lt;/code&gt; HTML global attribute"</code></li>
<li><code class="notranslate">"titleHTML"</code>: <code class="notranslate">'&lt;code&gt;&amp;lt;input type="number"&amp;gt;&lt;/code&gt; HTML attribute value'</code></li>
</ul>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
